WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.298 --> 00:00:03.618
(dramatic music)

00:00:03.618 --> 00:00:06.392
- Chemistry explains literally everything

00:00:06.392 --> 00:00:07.943
that is happening around you.

00:00:07.943 --> 00:00:10.747
The dry ice is taking the
thermal energy from the water.

00:00:10.747 --> 00:00:14.576
Unfortunately I instantaneously
get judged on my appearance.

00:00:14.576 --> 00:00:16.389
That is very frustrating for me.

00:00:16.389 --> 00:00:18.230
So, I'm gonna pick up my hot water.

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:19.740
I'm gonna come over here
and I’m gonna throw it

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.639
right into my bucket, okay?

00:00:21.639 --> 00:00:23.089
It means I have to work harder,

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:26.701
but at the end it is so,
so incredibly worth it.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:28.019
And one.

00:00:28.019 --> 00:00:29.570
(banging)

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:33.237
(children scream and cheer)

00:00:34.197 --> 00:00:36.947
(dramatic music)

00:00:38.502 --> 00:00:40.006
My name is Dr. Kate Biberdorf,

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:44.665
and I am a lecturer at the
University of Texas at Austin.

00:00:44.665 --> 00:00:46.247
I'm trying to break the stigma

00:00:46.247 --> 00:00:48.707
of what a stereotypical
scientist looks like,

00:00:48.707 --> 00:00:50.887
so my thing is I am not wearing a bow tie,

00:00:50.887 --> 00:00:52.279
I'm not wearing suspenders,

00:00:52.279 --> 00:00:54.228
I don't have some frumpy cardigan on,

00:00:54.228 --> 00:00:56.597
I'm just some regular girl
who likes to play with fire

00:00:56.597 --> 00:00:58.554
and I also really like designer shoes

00:00:58.554 --> 00:00:59.506
and that's okay.

00:00:59.506 --> 00:01:02.019
As the alginate hits the calcium chloride,

00:01:02.019 --> 00:01:03.078
the alginate would prefer

00:01:03.078 --> 00:01:05.329
to be with the two-plus charge calcium

00:01:05.329 --> 00:01:07.312
instead of the one-plus charge sodium

00:01:07.312 --> 00:01:08.645
and what happens

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:11.676
is we form gummy worms.

00:01:11.676 --> 00:01:12.853
It doesn't matter what you look like,

00:01:12.853 --> 00:01:15.270
any human can be a scientist.

00:01:18.638 --> 00:01:22.133
I definitely try to use
energy and excitement.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:24.252
I love this one.

00:01:24.252 --> 00:01:26.089
I do my best to try to reach students

00:01:26.089 --> 00:01:28.239
that might be intimidated by science.

00:01:28.239 --> 00:01:29.426
I use anything that will make

00:01:29.426 --> 00:01:32.005
the 483 students sit up straight

00:01:32.005 --> 00:01:34.472
and actually listen to the
words coming out of your mouth.

00:01:34.472 --> 00:01:37.095
(banging)

00:01:37.095 --> 00:01:39.027
As soon as I've exploded
something in their face,

00:01:39.027 --> 00:01:40.840
I have their attention for just 60 seconds

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:43.001
and I can do whatever I
can to shove that knowledge

00:01:43.001 --> 00:01:45.306
right into their brains.

00:01:45.306 --> 00:01:46.139
Ah, yay.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:50.337
Okay, so what we're gonna do today

00:01:50.337 --> 00:01:51.700
is learn some chemistry.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:53.963
We're going to do three
different hands-on experiments.

00:01:53.963 --> 00:01:57.917
I find chemistry to be an
incredibly challenging topic.

00:01:57.917 --> 00:01:59.543
Pour your water, pour your water.

00:01:59.543 --> 00:02:01.473
Beautiful, now keep
watching, keep watching.

00:02:01.473 --> 00:02:04.412
I'm so sick of the
stereotypical female scientist

00:02:04.412 --> 00:02:07.215
and we can do things other
than biology, by the way.

00:02:07.215 --> 00:02:09.999
Chemistry, physics,
engineering, we can do it.

00:02:09.999 --> 00:02:11.478
Look at what you made.

00:02:11.478 --> 00:02:13.436
The fact that I've been able to master it

00:02:13.436 --> 00:02:16.800
but then use science to
start the conversation

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.859
but then physically stand
there and break that image.

00:02:19.859 --> 00:02:21.614
It's the most rewarding thing

00:02:21.614 --> 00:02:23.447
I could ever do ever.

